Research and implement a message broker system optimized for UEP protocol validation. Based on current industry standards, NATS JetStream 2.10+ is recommended for its performance characteristics and support for subject-based filtering that aligns with UEP protocol validation needs.

Implementation steps:
1. Deploy NATS JetStream cluster with horizontal scaling capabilities
2. Implement UEP protocol validation as a NATS service that intercepts messages
3. Create UEP-specific subjects following the pattern `UEP.{version}.{agent}.{capability}`
4. Implement message schema validation using JSON Schema 2020-12 standard
5. Set up persistent streams for audit trails with configurable retention policies
6. Implement circuit breakers using NATS slow consumer detection
7. Configure monitoring using Prometheus and Grafana dashboards

Consider implementing a fallback mechanism using RabbitMQ 3.12+ with Shovel plugin for cross-datacenter replication if needed for enterprise deployments.

Code example for UEP message validation middleware:
```typescript
class UepMessageValidator {
  async validateMessage(msg: Msg, schema: JSONSchema7): Promise<boolean> {
    try {
      const payload = JSON.parse(msg.data.toString());
      const ajv = new Ajv({ strict: false });
      const validate = ajv.compile(schema);
      const valid = validate(payload);
      if (!valid) {
        await this.logViolation(msg, validate.errors);
        return false;
      }
      return true;
    } catch (error) {
      await this.logError(msg, error);
      return false;
    }
  }
}
```

